# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Alpaca API Configuration for Backtest Examples
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# This file contains environment variables needed for the Alpaca backtest examples.
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your actual API keys.
#
# IMPORTANT: Never commit your actual .env file with real API keys to version control!
#
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ================================
# ALPACA API CREDENTIALS (Required)
# ================================
# Get your API keys from: https://alpaca.markets/
# Steps:
#   1. Sign up for a free Alpaca account
#   2. Navigate to Paper Trading -> API Keys
#   3. Generate new API keys

ALPACA_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
ALPACA_API_SECRET=your_api_secret_here

# ================================
# NOTES
# ================================
#
# Historical Data Access:
# - Alpaca provides free historical data including:
#   - Trade ticks (individual trades)
#   - Quote ticks (NBBO - National Best Bid and Offer)
#   - Bars (1min, 5min, 15min, 1hour, 1day, 1week, 1month)
#
# - Data availability depends on your subscription:
#   - Free tier: IEX data
#   - Paid tier: SIP data (full real-time + historical)
#
# Tick Data Considerations:
# - Tick data can be very large (millions of ticks per day for active stocks)
# - The examples use shorter time periods to keep data size manageable
# - Consider using intraday bars if you need longer periods
#
# Example Data Sizes (approximate for AAPL):
# - 1 hour of trade ticks: ~10,000-50,000 ticks
# - 1 hour of quote ticks: ~100,000-500,000 quotes
# - 1 day of 1-minute bars: ~390 bars
